Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?perf=20phase=2011=20patch=200113=20=E2=80=94=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?off-screen=20tile=20bbox=20skip=20in=20FG-tilemap=20loop?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DOS-PORT (patch 0113, Phase 11 iter H opt #2). Pre-clip iteration
range in `_tilemap_render_uncached_full_loop` to the map-bounds-
clipped visible window when SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_TILE_BBOX_SKIP=1.
Eliminates per-iteration `(mapx+x) >= 0 && (mapx+x) < map.xsize &&
...` OOB bounds check AND skips OOB tiles entirely (no iterations
spent on tiles outside the map). Wave-22.5 measurement: ~30000
tiles visited / ~1900 drawn per 100 flips on PAUSE-equivalent state
(94% wasted iteration); this lever cuts the iteration overhead.

Killswitch: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_TILE_BBOX_SKIP=1 strict-1, default OFF
(iter H PLAY2 is the A/B opt-in test).

Mechanism: at FG-loop entry, compute clipped iteration range from
camera position + screen size + map bounds:
  x_loop_start          = max(0, -mapx)
  x_loop_end_inclusive  = min(x_max_inclusive, map.xsize - mapx - 1)
  y_loop_start          = max(0, -mapy)
  y_loop_end_inclusive  = min(y_max_inclusive, map.ysize - mapy - 1)
  blit_x_start         += x_loop_start * TILE_W   (preserve screen-
                                                   position alignment)
  blit_y               += y_loop_start * TILE_H

When env unset: clipped range = full bbox = existing behavior bit-
for-bit. Zero behavioral change (clean killswitch).

When env set: outer loops iterate ONLY in the clipped range. The
inner OOB bounds-check still present (tautologically true when
clipped; the clipped range is correctness-preserving), but redundant
in the ON path. Compiler may not eliminate the redundant check (vars
not constant-foldable across function boundary), so per-iter cost
of the redundant check remains. Real-HW W22-WB-H PLAY2 measures
actual fps gain -- primary gains come from skipped OOB iterations,
secondary gains from reduced branch-misprediction pressure.

Smoke (DOSBox-X-fast, A/B comparison with wave-25 instrumentation):

  Gate 1 -- env unset (baseline):
    [mds-tfg-tiles n=100 visited=37400 drawn_normal=1900
     drawn_special=0 skipped_attr=31700 skipped_oob=3800
     visit_overhead_per_tile_us=-1.51
     dispatch_overhead_per_tile_us=16.40]
    60 flips, no crashes.

  Gate 2 -- TILE_BBOX_SKIP=1:
    [mds-tfg-tiles n=100 visited=33600 drawn_normal=1900
     drawn_special=0 skipped_attr=31700 skipped_oob=0
     visit_overhead_per_tile_us=-1.71
     dispatch_overhead_per_tile_us=16.57]
    59 flips, no crashes.

  A/B math:
    37400 (off) - 33600 (on) = 3800 (the OOB iterations skipped)
    skipped_oob dropped from 3800 -> 0 in ON path (bbox-skip elides
                                                  all OOB iterations)
    drawn_normal + skipped_attr unchanged across modes (1900 +
                                                        31700 = 33600
                                                        in both)
                                                        -- correctness
                                                        preserved
                                                        (no in-bounds
                                                        tiles dropped)

  Self-check `visited == drawn_normal + drawn_special + skipped_attr
  + skipped_oob` holds in BOTH modes:
    OFF: 37400 = 1900 + 0 + 31700 + 3800 [OK]
    ON:  33600 = 1900 + 0 + 31700 + 0    [OK]

  Zero [mds-tfg-selfcheck WARN] lines in either gate.

  strings-grep verifies SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_TILE_BBOX_SKIP env-var
  symbol + tile_bbox_skip_active() function symbol present in
  binary.

  ~10% reduction in tile iterations under DOSBox-X. Real-HW W22-WB-H
  PLAY2 measures fps gain on g2k Pentium-OD-83. Per dispatch's "save
  2-4 ms / flip in mds_tilemap_fg" estimate.

NEW infrastructure:
  diagnostic_timers.h: tile_bbox_skip_active() forward-decl
  Renderer.cpp:
    - _abl_tile_bbox_skip() in anonymous namespace (strict-1
      cached static-const-bool per W22A/W22.5/W23 family pattern)
    - tile_bbox_skip_active() file-scope wrapper at end-of-file
      per W20B build-fix amendment placement

MODIFIED:
  map.cpp _tilemap_render_uncached_full_loop:
    - bbox_skip_on local read at function entry
    - x_loop_start / x_loop_end_inclusive / y_loop_start /
      y_loop_end_inclusive variables computed from camera + map
      bounds when bbox_skip_on; defaults to full-bbox when off
    - blit_x_start / blit_y adjusted to preserve screen-position
      alignment for clipped first column/row
    - Outer for-loops iterate clipped range; inner body unchanged
      (preserves wave-25 instrumentation + tile-category counter
      logic)
  docs/BOOT.md: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_TILE_BBOX_SKIP entry added

Out of scope (per silent_narrow_pattern.md):
  - In-loop bounds-check elimination (compiler may not const-fold;
    if real-HW iter shows insufficient gain, slot 0114a could split
    the body into two variants -- bounds-checked + bounds-known --
    keyed off bbox_skip_on)
  - mds_tilemap_bg loop bbox skip (BG = 3.77 ms / flip per W22.5;
    smaller slice; deferred until FG lever proven on real HW)
  - Pre-cached bbox state across consecutive frames (camera moves
    smoothly; could compute once per camera-update vs per-flip).
    Negligible compute cost (4 max/min ops per flip); not worth
    architectural complexity for slot 0113.
